## 3. UI Control Parameters

To cover all these genres smoothly, structure your UI controls into four main modules:

| Module | Key Parameters |
| --- | --- |
| **Grid & Subdivision** | Base Grid ($1/8$, $1/16$, $1/32$), Triplet Toggle, Polyrhythm Ratio ($3:4$, $5:4$, $7:8$), Roll Density Slider. |
| **Humanization & Timing** | Micro-Timing Shift ($\pm\text{ms}$), Swing % ($50\%$ straight to $75\%$ heavy triplet), Drunk/Jitter Variance, Laid-back Factor. |
| **Velocity & Dynamics** | Accent Weight, Ghost Note Suppression, Human Velocity Jitter, Pitch Decay on Rolls, Stereo Pan Spread. |
| **Articulation & Engine** | Hat Openness Slider ($0-100\%$), Choke Group Assign, Tip/Shank Morphing, Sample Layer Alternation (Round-Robin). |

